From 1e79df381369abc7d71da31c775acf26af7036ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:45:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Prose Portal: the guest answers the host

The host can type at this machine and photograph the result, and learn
nothing from it: a screenshot has no exit status in it, and every
host-side guess at "has it booted" is either true at 2.4 s -- when the
display driver sets the mode and the boot splash draws -- or true again
whenever the machine pauses for breath. Two fresh boots measured 18 s
apart under the best guess available from outside.

prose_portal answers instead. PING, RUN (a command line, returning its
exit status with stdout and stderr kept apart) and INFO (uptime, memory,
and whether Tracker and the Deskbar are running, which is what a caller
means by "booted").

Framed so the transport can change: a 16-byte header with a magic, a
version, a type, an id echoed in the reply, and a length. Today it is
carried by TCP on this machine's own network, which under
Virtualization.framework reaches no further than the Mac hosting it; a
virtio device is the eventual home and only the read and write calls move.

The switch is the wrong way round on purpose. The host cannot write a
file into this machine's disk before it has a channel to it, so a marker
the host must create first could never be created. The gate that matters
is on the host -- nothing connects unless the owner allowed automation --
and /boot/home/config/settings/prose/no-automation stops it listening
from the inside.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
